Z||000002||DJRice||12-15-1999||09:49 AM||||Dano, <P>Just out of curousity, what does the stalk with the delay wipers and cruise run (about) nowadays?  Are there others who make the replacement GM stalks as well?||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||12-15-1999||10:17 AM||||Dano... My 22p parts book should be ariving any day now. I will look up the part# as soon as I get it.Ross||||reg||1
Z||000004||GREENDANO||12-15-1999||05:29 PM||||To clarify... I need the switch in the column, not the stalk.  If I remeber correctly a GM stalk with delay is around $65-$70.  Not sure.  Local GM guys can give you an accurate price.  I get my discount, but it isn't cost effective for you or me to buy the parts and send them to you.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||07:00 PM||||Dan-o,<P>According to my 22P, a 2-spd switch was available on 84-85 & 86 cars.  The part numbers are 7841050 & 7841050 respectively.  Yes they are the same, but not listed as such.  It appears on 10.163 in my book that was published in 11/90.  The schematic is in group 6.518 although I can't find it in the diagram.  The unit proce is supposedly 53.75.  <P>Good Luck,<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>||||reg||3
Z||000006||GREENDANO||12-15-1999||09:42 PM||||I will verify the part number tomorrow to be sure.  I found only two switches listed.  According to the parts listing GM doesn't list a 2 speed switch with tilt column, which is what I have.  Am I missing something, did someone replace the stalk maybe.  Does anyone have the RPO # for delay wipers?  Maybe I just have the wrong stalk.  That would be cool to have delayed wipers like I had on my '85 GT.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||9
Z||000007||GREENDANO||12-16-1999||11:40 PM||||Looked up every RPO on my car.  For the record in case anyone was interested, the RPO for delayed wipers is CD4.  I do have delayed wipers, the previous owner must have put the wrong stalk on.  <BR>W_T, you gave me the correct part number, it's discontinued and noone on the GM parts locator has it.  Fortunately, I do have delay, so all I need is a new stalk.  <BR> Thanks everyone for the info!<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
